    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can explain math concepts in simple, relatable ways—like through stories or everyday examples. They can offer step-by-step guidance without pressure, helping students feel less anxious. In classrooms, they could act as tutors for individual learners, especially those who struggle. But they must be used with human teachers to ensure depth and emotional support, like in yoga or philosophy classes."
